== Ablutio | The Washing of the Altars
H: AD ALTARIA ABLUENDA
 = THE WASHING OF THE ALTARS
I: Ex Officio Triduo ante Pascha O.P. (1927), pp. 82-111.
 = From the Dominican Triduum book (1927), pp. 82-111.
R: Feria quinta in Cena Domini, post comestionem utriusque mensæ hora idonea, fiat signum cum tabula ad Altaria abluenda. Quo audito, Prælatus præparet se ad hoc Officium cum his Ministris, scilicet: Diacono, et Subdiacono, et Ceroferariis, et aliis duobus, quorum unus deferat situlam cum aqua, et alter scopam, ex aliquibus ramis arborum, et linteum, et hi omnes induantur albis: Priore et Diacono habentibus Stolas, et manipulos, et Subdiacono manipulum. Quibus præparatis, fiat secundum signum; et tunc Fratres conveniant in Choro, et sic præcedentibus Ceroferariis, et subsequentibus post eos illis qui aquam et scopam deferunt; deinde Subdiacono cum ampulla vinaria, et Diacono cum libello, quem tenere debet coram Priore ad Orationes dicendas, Prælatus procedat ad majus Altare abluendum; cumque illuc pervenerit, Cantor voce mediocri (in qua totum hoc Officium fieri debet) incipiat *℟. In monte Oliveti* cum suo ℣. Et Conventus utrumque prosequatur, cum resumptione: quod etiam in ceteris Responsoriis cantandis ad hoc Officium observetur.
 = On Maundy Thursday, after the meal at both tables, at a suitable hour the signal is given with the board for the washing of the altars. When it is heard, the Prelate prepares himself for this Office with these ministers: the Deacon, the Subdeacon, the Candle-bearers, and two others, one of whom carries a bucket of water and the other a broom made of branches of trees, and a towel; all of them wear albs, the Prior and the Deacon with stoles and maniples, the Subdeacon with a maniple. When they are ready the second signal is given, and the brethren assemble in Choir. Then, the Candle-bearers going first, followed by those who carry the water and the broom, then the Subdeacon with the cruet of wine and the Deacon with the little book, which he is to hold before the Prior for saying the Prayers, the Prelate goes to wash the high altar. When he arrives there, the Cantor in a moderate voice (in which this whole Office is to be done) begins *℟. In monte Oliveti* with its ℣., and the Community continues both, with the repeat; which is to be observed also in singing the other Responsories of this Office.
G: op-abl-r01 | In monte Olivéti · Responsorium I
R: Dum cantatur ℟. primum: *In monte*, qui situlam defert, effundat aquam super magnam mensam Altaris, si consecrata fuerit, vel super mensam Altaris portatilis, si Altare non fuerit consecratum: quo facto, Prior accipiens scopam, ea lavet Altare; deinde a Fratre deferente linteum extergatur: postmodum Prior scopam Fratri reddat, et accepta ampulla de manu Subdiaconi, in modum crucis vinum effundat super Altare. Finito Responsorio, Cantor incipiat Antiphonam de Sancto, vel Sanctis illis, in cujus vel quorum memoriam Altare constructum est, et Conventus ipsam prosequatur: qua finita, Ceroferarii (Cantore eis deferente) dicant ℣. de Sancto, vel Sanctis illis, et Prior Orationem ex libello, quem coram ipso tenebit Diaconus. Deinde procedatur ad cetera Altaria, quæ sunt in Ecclesia. Eodem modo fiat per singula Altaria, Cantore, post terminationem Orationis, incipiente immediate singula ℟℟. secundum ordinem ipsorum, dum procedunt ad singula Altaria: deinde Antiphona de Sancto, vel Sanctis, et ℣. et Oratio, ut prædictum est, dicantur.
 = While the first Responsory *In monte* is sung, the one who carries the bucket pours water over the large table of the altar, if it is consecrated, or over the table of the portable altar, if the altar is not consecrated; this done, the Prior takes the broom and washes the altar with it; then it is wiped dry by the brother who carries the towel. Afterwards the Prior gives the broom back to the brother and, taking the cruet from the Subdeacon's hand, pours the wine over the altar in the form of a cross. When the Responsory is finished, the Cantor begins the Antiphon of the Saint or Saints in whose memory the altar is built, and the Community continues it; when it is finished, the Candle-bearers (the Cantor giving it to them) say the ℣. of the Saint or Saints, and the Prior the Prayer from the little book, which the Deacon holds before him. Then they go on to the other altars in the church. The same is done at each altar, the Cantor, when the Prayer is ended, at once beginning the Responsories one by one in their order, while they go to each altar; then the Antiphon of the Saint or Saints, the ℣. and the Prayer are said, as above.
R: Ubi aptitudo loci permiserit, præcedente Priore cum Ministris ad Altaria, Conventus cantando Responsoria gregatim sequatur: et ad Altare, quod lavatur, seorsim ℣. cum Antiphona cantetur. Si vero non fuerit locus ad procedendum idoneus, Prælatus cum Ministris ad Altaria procedat: et quæ cantanda sunt a Conventu, in Choro cantentur.
 = Where the place allows, the Prior going ahead with the ministers to the altars, the Community follows in a body singing the Responsories, and at the altar being washed the ℣. with the Antiphon is sung apart. But if the place is not suitable for a procession, the Prelate goes to the altars with the ministers, and what the Community is to sing is sung in Choir.
G: op-abl-r02 | Tristis est ánima mea · Responsorium II
G: op-abl-r03 | Ecce vídimus eum · Responsorium III
G: op-abl-r04 | Amícus meus · Responsorium IV
G: op-abl-r05 | Unus ex vobis · Responsorium V
G: op-abl-r06 | Eram quasi agnus · Responsorium VI
G: op-abl-r07 | Una hora · Responsorium VII
G: op-abl-r08 | Senióres pópuli · Responsorium VIII
G: op-abl-r09 | Revelábunt cæli · Responsorium IX
R: Cum ad ultimum Altare procedendum fuerit, inchoetur *℟. Circumdederunt*. Et si Altaria fuerint plura quam decem, dicto *℟. Revelabunt*, resumantur de antedictis, prout necesse fuerit: et ad ultimum Altare, *℟. Circumdederunt*, reservetur. Si vero pauciora fuerint Altaria quam Responsoria, cantentur tot quot necessaria fuerint, reliqua intermittantur, et *℟. Circumdederunt*, ultimo cantetur:
 = When they are to go to the last altar, *℟. Circumdederunt* is begun. If there are more than ten altars, after *℟. Revelabunt* the foregoing are taken up again as needed, and *℟. Circumdederunt* is kept for the last altar. If there are fewer altars than Responsories, as many are sung as are needed, the rest are left out, and *℟. Circumdederunt* is sung last:
G: op-abl-r10 | Circumdedérunt me · Responsorium X
H: ANTIPHONÆ, VERSICULI ET ORATIONES
 = ANTIPHONS, VERSICLES AND PRAYERS
R: In Altarium ablutione cantandæ, non eo ordine quo collocatæ sunt, sed juxta Altarium dispositionem in quolibet Conventu. Si aliquis Conventus habet alia privata Altaria quæ hic notata non sint, poterunt pro eis accipi Antiphonæ de Communi. Ad Altare Majus dicatur Antiphona, et Oratio Titularis Ecclesiæ.
 = To be sung at the washing of the altars, not in the order in which they are placed here, but according to the arrangement of the altars in each convent. If a convent has other private altars that are not given here, the Antiphons of the Common may be taken for them. At the high altar the Antiphon and Prayer of the Titular of the church are said.
F: Ad Altare Sanctissimi Crucifixi | At the altar of the Holy Crucifix
G: op-abl-a01 | Tuam Crucem · Antiphona I
T: {℣.} Dícite in natiónibus. {℟.} Quia Dóminus regnávit a ligno.
 = {℣.} Say among the nations. {℟.} That the Lord hath reigned from the wood.
L: Orémus
 = Let us pray
T: ^Deus, qui pro nobis Fílium tuum Crucis patíbulum subíre voluísti, ut inimíci a nobis expélleres potestátem: concéde nobis fámulis tuis, ut resurrectiónis grátiam consequámur. Per eúndem Christum.
 = O God, who didst will that thy Son should undergo the gibbet of the Cross for us, that thou mightest drive from us the power of the enemy: grant to us thy servants that we may attain the grace of the resurrection. Through the same Christ.
F/
F: Ad Altare Sanctissimi Nominis Jesu | At the altar of the Holy Name of Jesus
G: op-abl-a02 | Sit nomen Dómini · Antiphona VII
T: {℣.} In nómine Jesu omne genu flectátur. {℟.} Cæléstium, terréstrium, et infernórum.
 = {℣.} At the name of Jesus let every knee bow. {℟.} Of those in heaven, on earth, and under the earth.
L: Orémus
 = Let us pray
T: ^Sancti nóminis tui, Dómine, timórem páriter et amórem fac nos habére perpétuum: quia numquam tua gubernatióne destítuis, quos in soliditáte tuæ dilectiónis instítuis. Per Christum.
 = Make us, O Lord, to have a perpetual fear and love of thy holy name: for thou never failest to govern those whom thou dost establish in the firmness of thy love. Through Christ.
F/
F: Ad Altare Sacratissimi Cordis Jesu | At the altar of the Sacred Heart of Jesus
G: op-abl-a03 | Suscépit nos Dóminus · Antiphona VII
T: {℣.} Miserátor, et miséricors Dóminus. {℟.} Longánimis, et multum miséricors.
 = {℣.} The Lord is compassionate and merciful. {℟.} Long-suffering and plenteous in mercy.
L: Orémus
 = Let us pray
T: ^Fac nos, Dómine Jesu, sanctíssimi Cordis tui virtútibus índui, et afféctibus inflammári: ut et imágini bonitátis tuæ confórmes, et tuæ redemptiónis mereámur esse partícipes: Qui vivis.
 = Grant us, Lord Jesus, to be clothed with the virtues of thy most holy Heart and inflamed with its affections: that, conformed to the image of thy goodness, we may be worthy to share in thy redemption: Who livest.
F/
F: Ad Altare Sacratissimi Rosarii | At the altar of the Most Holy Rosary
G: op-abl-a04 | Speciósa facta est · Antiphona V
T: {℣.} Regína sacratíssimi Rosárii, ora pro nobis. {℟.} Ut digni efficiámur promissiónibus Christi.
 = {℣.} Queen of the most holy Rosary, pray for us. {℟.} That we may be made worthy of the promises of Christ.
L: Orémus
 = Let us pray
T: ^Deus, cujus Unigénitus per vitam, mortem et resurrectiónem suam nobis salútis ætérnæ prǽmia comparávit: concéde, quǽsumus, ut hæc mystéria sanctíssimo Rosário beátæ Maríæ Vírginis recoléntes, et imitémur quod cóntinent, et quod promíttunt assequámur. Per eúndem Christum.
 = O God, whose only-begotten Son by his life, death and resurrection hath purchased for us the rewards of eternal salvation: grant, we beseech thee, that meditating on these mysteries in the most holy Rosary of the Blessed Virgin Mary, we may both imitate what they contain and obtain what they promise. Through the same Christ.
F/
F: Ad Altare Immaculatæ Conceptionis B. V. Mariæ | At the altar of the Immaculate Conception
G: op-abl-a05 | Tota pulchra es · Antiphona VII
T: {℣.} In Conceptióne tua immaculáta, Dei Génitrix, Virgo. {℟.} Cæli et terra læténtur.
 = {℣.} In thy immaculate Conception, Mother of God, Virgin. {℟.} Let heaven and earth rejoice.
L: Orémus
 = Let us pray
T: ^Deus, qui per immaculátam Vírginis Conceptiónem dignum Fílio tuo habitáculum præparásti: quǽsumus, ut qui ex morte ejúsdem Fílii tui prævísa eam ab omni labe præservásti, nos quoque mundos ejus intercessióne ad te perveníre concédas. Per eúndem Christum.
 = O God, who by the immaculate Conception of the Virgin didst prepare a worthy dwelling for thy Son: we beseech thee that, as by the foreseen death of the same thy Son thou didst preserve her from every stain, so thou wouldst grant us also, made clean by her intercession, to come to thee. Through the same Christ.
F/
F: Ad aliud Altare Beatissimæ Virginis | At another altar of the Blessed Virgin
G: op-abl-a06 | Sancta Dei Génitrix · Antiphona I
T: {℣.} Ora pro nobis, sancta Dei Génitrix. {℟.} Ut digni efficiámur promissiónibus Christi.
 = {℣.} Pray for us, holy Mother of God. {℟.} That we may be made worthy of the promises of Christ.
L: Orémus
 = Let us pray
T: ^Prótege, Dómine, fámulos tuos subsídiis pacis: et beátæ Maríæ semper Vírginis patrocíniis confidéntes, a cunctis hóstibus redde secúros. Per Christum.
 = Protect thy servants, O Lord, with the help of peace; and make them, trusting in the patronage of blessed Mary ever Virgin, safe from all enemies. Through Christ.
F/
F: Ad Altare Sanctorum Angelorum | At the altar of the Holy Angels
G: op-abl-a07 | Archángeli Michaélis · Antiphona I
T: {℣.} Adoráte Deum. {℟.} Omnes Ángeli ejus.
 = {℣.} Adore God. {℟.} All you his Angels.
L: Orémus
 = Let us pray
T: ^Deus, qui miro órdine Angelórum ministéria hominúmque dispénsas: concéde propítius; ut a quibus tibi ministrántibus in cælo semper assístitur, ab his in terra vita nostra muniátur. Per Christum.
 = O God, who in a wonderful order dost dispense the ministries of Angels and men: mercifully grant that our life on earth may be defended by those who stand ever ministering to thee in heaven. Through Christ.
F/
F: Ad Altare S. Joannis Baptistæ | At the altar of St John the Baptist
G: op-abl-a08 | Inter natos mulíerum · Antiphona III
T: {℣.} Fuit homo missus a Deo. {℟.} Cui nomen erat Joánnes.
 = {℣.} There was a man sent from God. {℟.} Whose name was John.
L: Orémus
 = Let us pray
T: ^Præsta, quǽsumus, omnípotens Deus: ut família tua per viam salútis incédat; et beáti Joánnis Præcursóris hortaménta sectándo, ad eum, quem prædíxit, secúra pervéniat. Per Christum Dóminum nostrum.
 = Grant, we beseech thee, almighty God, that thy family may walk in the way of salvation and, following the exhortations of blessed John the Forerunner, may come safely to him whom he foretold. Through Christ our Lord.
F/
F: Ad Altare S. Joseph, Sponsi Beatæ Mariæ Virginis | At the altar of St Joseph, Spouse of the Blessed Virgin Mary
G: op-abl-a09 | Ecce fidélis servus · Antiphona III
T: {℣.} Amávit eum Dóminus et ornávit eum. {℟.} Stolam glóriæ índuit eum.
 = {℣.} The Lord loved him and adorned him. {℟.} He clothed him with a robe of glory.
L: Orémus
 = Let us pray
T: ^Beáti Patriárchæ Joseph, sanctíssimæ Genitrícis tuæ Sponsi, quǽsumus, Dómine, méritis adjuvémur: ut quod possibílitas nostra non óbtinet, ejus nobis intercessióne donétur: Qui vivis.
 = May we be helped, O Lord, we beseech thee, by the merits of the blessed Patriarch Joseph, Spouse of thy most holy Mother: that what our own power cannot obtain may be given us by his intercession: Who livest.
F/
F: Ad Altare S. Petri Apostoli | At the altar of St Peter the Apostle
G: op-abl-a10 | Petre, amas me · Antiphona IV
T: {℣.} Tu es Petrus. {℟.} Et super hanc petram ædificábo Ecclésiam meam.
 = {℣.} Thou art Peter. {℟.} And upon this rock I will build my Church.
L: Orémus
 = Let us pray
T: ^Deus, qui beáto Petro Apóstolo tuo, collátis clávibus regni cæléstis, ligándi atque solvéndi pontifícium tradidísti: concéde, ut intercessiónis ejus auxílio, a peccatórum nostrórum néxibus liberémur: Qui vivis.
 = O God, who, giving to blessed Peter thy Apostle the keys of the kingdom of heaven, didst bestow on him the pontifical power of binding and loosing: grant that by the help of his intercession we may be freed from the bonds of our sins: Who livest.
F/
F: Ad Altare S. Pauli Apostoli | At the altar of St Paul the Apostle
G: op-abl-a11 | Sancte Paule Apóstole · Antiphona VIII
T: {℣.} Tu es vas electiónis, sancte Paule Apóstole. {℟.} Prædicátor veritátis in univérso mundo.
 = {℣.} Thou art a vessel of election, holy Apostle Paul. {℟.} A preacher of truth in the whole world.
L: Orémus
 = Let us pray
T: ^Deus, qui multitúdinem géntium beáti Pauli Apóstoli prædicatióne docuísti: da nobis, quǽsumus, ut cujus memóriam cólimus, ejus apud te patrocínia sentiámus. Per Christum.
 = O God, who didst teach a multitude of nations by the preaching of blessed Paul the Apostle: grant us, we beseech thee, that we who honour his memory may feel his patronage with thee. Through Christ.
F/
F: Ad Altare S. Dominici P. N. | At the altar of our Holy Father St Dominic
G: op-abl-a12 | Pie Pater Domínice · Antiphona I
T: {℣.} Ora pro nobis, beáte Pater Domínice. {℟.} Ut digni efficiámur promissiónibus Christi.
 = {℣.} Pray for us, blessed Father Dominic. {℟.} That we may be made worthy of the promises of Christ.
L: Orémus
 = Let us pray
T: ^Deus, qui Ecclésiam tuam beáti Domínici Confessóris tui Patris nostri illumináre dignátus es méritis et doctrínis: concéde, ut ejus intercessióne temporálibus non destituátur auxíliis, et spirituálibus semper profíciat increméntis. Per Christum.
 = O God, who didst deign to enlighten thy Church by the merits and teaching of blessed Dominic thy Confessor, our Father: grant that by his intercession she may not be deprived of temporal help, and may ever advance in spiritual growth. Through Christ.
F/
F: Ad Altare S. Petri Martyris | At the altar of St Peter Martyr
G: op-abl-a13 | Petrus novus íncola · Antiphona I
T: {℣.} Ora pro nobis, beáte Petre. {℟.} Ut digni efficiámur promissiónibus Christi.
 = {℣.} Pray for us, blessed Peter. {℟.} That we may be made worthy of the promises of Christ.
L: Orémus
 = Let us pray
T: ^Præsta, quǽsumus, omnípotens Deus: ut beáti Petri Mártyris tui fidem cóngrua devotióne sectémur; qui, pro ejúsdem fídei dilatatióne, martýrii palmam méruit obtinére. Per Christum.
 = Grant, we beseech thee, almighty God, that we may follow with fitting devotion the faith of blessed Peter thy Martyr, who for the spreading of that same faith was found worthy to win the palm of martyrdom. Through Christ.
F/
F: Ad Altare SS. Joannis et Soc. Mart. Gorcomiensium | At the altar of SS. John and Companions, Martyrs of Gorkum
G: op-abl-a14 | Exaltávit Dóminus · Antiphona VII
T: {℣.} Ora pro nobis, beáte Joánnes, cum sóciis tuis. {℟.} Ut digni efficiámur promissiónibus Christi.
 = {℣.} Pray for us, blessed John, with thy companions. {℟.} That we may be made worthy of the promises of Christ.
L: Orémus
 = Let us pray
T: ^Deus, qui beatórum Mártyrum tuórum Joánnis, et Sociórum ejus pro fide tua certámen æternitátis láurea decorásti: concéde propítius, ut eórum méritis et imitatióne certántes in terris, cum ipsis coronári mereámur in cælis. Per Christum.
 = O God, who didst crown with the laurel of eternity the combat of thy blessed Martyrs John and his Companions for thy faith: mercifully grant that, striving on earth by their merits and example, we may be worthy to be crowned with them in heaven. Through Christ.
F/
F: Ad Altare S. Pii V | At the altar of St Pius V
G: op-abl-a15 | Pius instar facis · Antiphona II
T: {℣.} Ora pro nobis, beáte Pie. {℟.} Ut digni efficiámur promissiónibus Christi.
 = {℣.} Pray for us, blessed Pius. {℟.} That we may be made worthy of the promises of Christ.
L: Orémus
 = Let us pray
T: ^Deus, qui ad conteréndos Ecclésiæ tuæ hostes, et ad divínum cultum reparándum, beátum Pium Pontíficem Máximum elígere dignátus es: fac nos ipsíus deféndi præsídiis, et ita tuis inhærére obséquiis; ut, ómnium hóstium superátis insídiis, perpétua pace lætémur. Per Christum.
 = O God, who didst deign to choose blessed Pius as Supreme Pontiff to crush the enemies of thy Church and to restore divine worship: grant that we may be defended by his protection and so cleave to thy service that, overcoming the snares of all our enemies, we may rejoice in everlasting peace. Through Christ.
F/
F: Ad Altare S. Antonini Archiep. Florentini | At the altar of St Antoninus, Archbishop of Florence
G: op-abl-a16 | Beátus Antonínus · Antiphona VIII
T: {℣.} Ora pro nobis, beáte Antoníne. {℟.} Ut digni efficiámur promissiónibus Christi.
 = {℣.} Pray for us, blessed Antoninus. {℟.} That we may be made worthy of the promises of Christ.
L: Orémus
 = Let us pray
T: ^Sancti Antoníni, Dómine, Confessóris tui atque Pontíficis méritis adjuvémur: ut sicut te in illo mirábilem prædicámus, ita in nos misericórdem fuísse gloriémur. Per Christum.
 = May we be helped, O Lord, by the merits of Saint Antoninus, thy Confessor and Bishop: that as we proclaim thee wonderful in him, so we may glory that thou hast been merciful to us. Through Christ.
F/
F: Ad Altare S. Thomæ de Aquino | At the altar of St Thomas Aquinas
G: op-abl-a17 | O Thoma, laus et glória · Antiphona I
T: {℣.} Ora pro nobis, beáte Thoma. {℟.} Ut digni efficiámur promissiónibus Christi.
 = {℣.} Pray for us, blessed Thomas. {℟.} That we may be made worthy of the promises of Christ.
L: Orémus
 = Let us pray
T: ^Deus, qui Ecclésiam tuam beáti Thomæ Confessóris tui atque Doctóris mira eruditióne claríficas, et sancta operatióne fecúndas: da nobis, quǽsumus, et quæ dócuit, intelléctu conspícere, et quæ egit, imitatióne complére. Per Christum.
 = O God, who dost enlighten thy Church by the wonderful learning of blessed Thomas thy Confessor and Doctor, and make her fruitful by his holy works: grant us, we beseech thee, both to understand what he taught and to fulfil by imitation what he did. Through Christ.
F/
F: Ad Altare S. Vincentii Confessoris | At the altar of St Vincent Ferrer
G: op-abl-a18 | Adsit nobis propítius · Antiphona I
T: {℣.} Ora pro nobis, beáte Vincénti. {℟.} Ut digni efficiámur promissiónibus Christi.
 = {℣.} Pray for us, blessed Vincent. {℟.} That we may be made worthy of the promises of Christ.
L: Orémus
 = Let us pray
T: ^Deus, qui géntium multitúdinem mira beáti Vincéntii Confessóris tui prædicatióne ad agnitiónem tui nóminis veníre tribuísti: præsta, quǽsumus, ut quem ventúrum júdicem nuntiávit in terris, præmiatórem habére mereámur in cælis: Christum Dóminum nostrum.
 = O God, who by the wonderful preaching of blessed Vincent thy Confessor didst bring a multitude of nations to the knowledge of thy name: grant, we beseech thee, that him whom he proclaimed on earth as the Judge to come we may be worthy to have in heaven as our rewarder: Christ our Lord.
F/
F: Ad Altare S. Hyacinthi Confessoris | At the altar of St Hyacinth
G: op-abl-a19 | Tuum, Dómine · Antiphona II
T: {℣.} Ora pro nobis, beáte Hyacínthe. {℟.} Ut digni efficiámur promissiónibus Christi.
 = {℣.} Pray for us, blessed Hyacinth. {℟.} That we may be made worthy of the promises of Christ.
L: Orémus
 = Let us pray
T: ^Deus, qui beátum Hyacínthum Confessórem tuum in divérsis natiónum pópulis óperum sanctitáte et miraculórum glória fecísti conspícuum: da nobis, ut ejus in mélius reformémur exémplis, et in advérsis protegámur auxíliis. Per Christum Dóminum nostrum.
 = O God, who didst make blessed Hyacinth thy Confessor renowned among the peoples of many nations by the holiness of his works and the glory of his miracles: grant that we may be reformed for the better by his example and protected in adversity by his help. Through Christ our Lord.
F/
F: Ad Altare S. Raymundi Confessoris | At the altar of St Raymond of Peñafort
G: op-abl-a20 | Piis Raymúndi précibus · Antiphona I
T: {℣.} Ora pro nobis, beáte Raymúnde. {℟.} Ut digni efficiámur promissiónibus Christi.
 = {℣.} Pray for us, blessed Raymond. {℟.} That we may be made worthy of the promises of Christ.
L: Orémus
 = Let us pray
T: ^Deus, qui beátum Raymúndum Pœniténtiæ sacraménti insígnem minístrum elegísti, et per maris undas mirabíliter traduxísti: concéde, ut ejus intercessióne dignos pœniténtiæ fructus fácere, et ad ætérnæ salútis portum perveníre valeámus. Per Christum.
 = O God, who didst choose blessed Raymond as an eminent minister of the sacrament of Penance and didst wondrously carry him over the waves of the sea: grant that by his intercession we may bring forth worthy fruits of penance and come to the harbour of eternal salvation. Through Christ.
F/
F: Ad Altare S. Ludovici Bertrandi Confessoris | At the altar of St Louis Bertrand
G: op-abl-a21 | Quasi meridiánus fulgor · Antiphona I
T: {℣.} Ora pro nobis, beáte Ludovíce. {℟.} Ut digni efficiámur promissiónibus Christi.
 = {℣.} Pray for us, blessed Louis. {℟.} That we may be made worthy of the promises of Christ.
L: Orémus
 = Let us pray
T: ^Deus, qui beátum Ludovícum Confessórem tuum per córporis mortificatiónem, et fídei præcónium, Sanctórum glóriæ coæquásti: præsta, ut quod fide profitémur, pietátis opéribus júgiter impleámus. Per Christum.
 = O God, who through the mortification of the body and the preaching of the faith didst make blessed Louis thy Confessor equal to the glory of the Saints: grant that what we profess by faith we may ever fulfil by works of piety. Through Christ.
F/
F: Ad Altare S. Catharinæ Senensis | At the altar of St Catherine of Siena
G: op-abl-a22 | Ad sedes regni · Antiphona IV
T: {℣.} Ora pro nobis, beáta Catharína. {℟.} Ut digni efficiámur promissiónibus Christi.
 = {℣.} Pray for us, blessed Catherine. {℟.} That we may be made worthy of the promises of Christ.
L: Orémus
 = Let us pray
T: ^Deus, qui beátæ Catharínæ, virginitátis et patiéntiæ speciáli privilégio decorátæ, malignántium spirítuum certámina víncere et in amóre tui nóminis inconcússe permanére tribuísti: concéde, quǽsumus, ut ejus imitatióne, calcáta mundi nequítia et ómnium hóstium superátis insídiis, ad tuam secúre glóriam transeámus. Per Christum.
 = O God, who didst grant to blessed Catherine, adorned with the special privilege of virginity and patience, to overcome the assaults of evil spirits and to remain unshaken in the love of thy name: grant, we beseech thee, that following her example, treading underfoot the wickedness of the world and overcoming the snares of all our enemies, we may pass safely to thy glory. Through Christ.
F/
F: Ad Altare S. Rosæ Limensis | At the altar of St Rose of Lima
G: op-abl-a23 | Rosa soror nostra · Antiphona VIII
T: {℣.} Ora pro nobis, beáta Rosa. {℟.} Ut digni efficiámur promissiónibus Christi.
 = {℣.} Pray for us, blessed Rose. {℟.} That we may be made worthy of the promises of Christ.
L: Orémus
 = Let us pray
T: ^Bonórum ómnium largítor, omnípotens Deus, qui beátam Rosam, cæléstis grátiæ rore prævéntam, virginitátis, et patiéntiæ decóre Indis floréscere voluísti: da nobis fámulis tuis, ut in odórem suavitátis ejus curréntes, Christi bonus odor éffici mereámur: Per eúndem Christum.
 = Almighty God, giver of all good things, who didst will that blessed Rose, forestalled by the dew of heavenly grace, should blossom in the Indies with the beauty of virginity and patience: grant to us thy servants that, running in the odour of her sweetness, we may be worthy to become the good odour of Christ: Through the same Christ.
F/
F: Ad Altare S. Agnetis de Monte Politiano | At the altar of St Agnes of Montepulciano
G: op-abl-a24 | Tuam laudántes glóriam · Antiphona II
T: {℣.} Ora pro nobis, beáta Agnes. {℟.} Ut digni efficiámur promissiónibus Christi.
 = {℣.} Pray for us, blessed Agnes. {℟.} That we may be made worthy of the promises of Christ.
L: Orémus
 = Let us pray
T: ^Deus, qui beátam Agnétem Vírginem tuam cælésti rore sæpe perfúndere, et oratiónis ejus loca divérsis enátis flóribus decoráre dignátus es: concéde propítius, ut ejus précibus perpétuo tuæ benedictiónis rore conspérsi, æternitátis fructus percípere mereámur. Per Christum.
 = O God, who didst deign often to bedew blessed Agnes thy Virgin with heavenly dew, and to adorn the places of her prayer with flowers of every kind springing up: mercifully grant that, sprinkled by her prayers with the dew of thy blessing for ever, we may be worthy to gather the fruits of eternity. Through Christ.
F/
F: Ad Altare S. Catharinæ de Ricciis | At the altar of St Catherine de' Ricci
G: op-abl-a25 | Exsultávit ánima mea · Antiphona VIII
T: {℣.} Ora pro nobis, beáta Catharína. {℟.} Ut digni efficiámur promissiónibus Christi.
 = {℣.} Pray for us, blessed Catherine. {℟.} That we may be made worthy of the promises of Christ.
L: Orémus
 = Let us pray
T: ^Dómine Jesu Christe, qui beátam Catharínam Vírginem tui amóre succénsam Passiónis contemplatióne claréscere voluísti: ejus intercessióne concéde, ut Passiónis mystéria devóte recoléntes, ejus fructum percípere mereámur: Qui vivis.
 = Lord Jesus Christ, who didst will that blessed Catherine thy Virgin, kindled with thy love, should shine by contemplation of thy Passion: grant by her intercession that, devoutly recalling the mysteries of the Passion, we may be worthy to gather its fruit: Who livest.
F/
F: Ad Altare Omnium Sanctorum O. N. | At the altar of All Saints of our Order
G: op-abl-a26 | Sanctos suos · Antiphona V
T: {℣.} Oráte pro nobis, Sancti et Sanctæ Dei. {℟.} Ut digni efficiámur promissiónibus Christi.
 = {℣.} Pray for us, all you Saints of God. {℟.} That we may be made worthy of the promises of Christ.
L: Orémus
 = Let us pray
T: ^Deus, qui Prædicatórum Ordinem copiósa Sanctórum sóbole fecundáre dignátus es, atque in ipsis heróica ómnium virtútum mérita sublímiter coronásti: da nobis illórum sequi vestígia; ut quos venerámur in terris, iis perpétua tandem festivitáte associémur in cælis. Per Christum.
 = O God, who didst deign to make the Order of Preachers fruitful with an abundant offspring of Saints, and in them didst crown on high the heroic merits of every virtue: grant us to follow in their footsteps, that we may at last be joined in everlasting festivity in heaven to those whom we venerate on earth. Through Christ.
F/
F: Ad Altare S. Mariæ Magdalenæ | At the altar of St Mary Magdalen
G: op-abl-a27 | Intercéde súpplicans · Antiphona V
T: {℣.} Óptimam partem elégit sibi María. {℟.} Quæ non auferétur ab ea.
 = {℣.} Mary hath chosen the best part. {℟.} Which shall not be taken from her.
L: Orémus
 = Let us pray
T: ^Largíre nobis, clementíssime Pater: ut sicut beáta María Magdaléna Dóminum nostrum Jesum Christum super ómnia diligéndo suórum óbtinuit véniam peccatórum; ita nobis apud misericórdiam tuam sempitérnam ímpetret beatitúdinem. Per eúndem Christum.
 = Grant to us, most merciful Father, that as blessed Mary Magdalen, by loving our Lord Jesus Christ above all things, obtained pardon for her sins, so she may obtain for us from thy mercy everlasting happiness. Through the same Christ.
F/
F: Ad Altare unius vel plurium Apostolorum | At the altar of one or more Apostles
G: op-abl-a28 | Estóte fortes in bello · Antiphona I
T: {℣.} In omnem terram exívit sonus eórum. {℟.} Et in fines orbis terræ verba eórum.
 = {℣.} Their sound hath gone forth into all the earth. {℟.} And their words unto the ends of the world.
L: Orémus
 = Let us pray
T: ^Prótege, Dómine, pópulum tuum: et Apóstoli tui N. (vel Apostolórum tuórum N. et N.) patrocínio (vel patrocíniis) confidéntem, perpétua defensióne consérva. Per Christum.
 = Protect thy people, O Lord, and keep them with continual defence as they trust in the patronage of thy Apostle N. (or of thy Apostles N. and N.). Through Christ.
F/
F: Ad Altare unius Martyris | At the altar of one Martyr
G: op-abl-a29 | Qui me conféssus fúerit · Antiphona I
T: {℣.} Glória et honóre coronásti eum, Dómine. {℟.} Et constituísti eum super ópera mánuum tuárum.
 = {℣.} Thou hast crowned him with glory and honour, O Lord. {℟.} And hast set him over the works of thy hands.
L: Orémus
 = Let us pray
T: ^Adésto, Dómine, supplicatiónibus nostris: ut qui ex iniquitáte nostra reos nos esse cognóscimus, beáti N. Mártyris tui (atque Pontíficis, si fuerit Pontifex) intercessióne liberémur. Per Christum Dóminum nostrum.
 = Be present, O Lord, to our supplications: that we who know ourselves guilty through our iniquity may be delivered by the intercession of blessed N. thy Martyr (and Bishop, if he was a bishop). Through Christ our Lord.
F/
F: Ad Altare plurium Martyrum | At the altar of several Martyrs
G: op-abl-a30 | Justórum ánimæ · Antiphona VII
T: {℣.} Lætámini in Dómino, et exsultáte justi. {℟.} Et gloriámini omnes recti corde.
 = {℣.} Be glad in the Lord and rejoice, ye just. {℟.} And glory, all ye right of heart.
L: Orémus
 = Let us pray
T: ^Præsta, quǽsumus, omnípotens Deus: ut qui gloriósos Mártyres fortes in sua confessióne cognóvimus, pios apud te in nostra intercessióne sentiámus. Per Christum.
 = Grant, we beseech thee, almighty God, that we who have known the glorious Martyrs as steadfast in their confession may feel them gracious with thee in interceding for us. Through Christ.
F/
F: Ad Altare unius Confessoris | At the altar of one Confessor
G: op-abl-a31 | Similábo eum · Antiphona I
T: {℣.} Amávit eum Dóminus, et ornávit eum. {℟.} Stolam glóriæ índuit eum.
 = {℣.} The Lord loved him and adorned him. {℟.} He clothed him with a robe of glory.
L: Orémus
 = Let us pray
T: ^Exáudi, Dómine, preces nostras: et interveniénte beáto N. Confessóre tuo (si fuerit Pontifex, atque Pontífice), supplicatiónes nostras placátus inténde. Per Christum.
 = Hear our prayers, O Lord, and, blessed N. thy Confessor (and Bishop, if he was a bishop) interceding, look graciously on our supplications. Through Christ.
F/
F: Ad Altare unius Doctoris | At the altar of one Doctor
L: Orémus
 = Let us pray
T: ^Deus, qui pópulo tuo ætérnæ salútis beátum N. minístrum tribuísti: præsta, quǽsumus, ut quem Doctórem vitæ habúimus in terris, intercessórem habére mereámur in cælis. Per Christum.
 = O God, who didst give blessed N. to thy people as a minister of eternal salvation: grant, we beseech thee, that we may be worthy to have as our intercessor in heaven him whom we had on earth as the teacher of life. Through Christ.
F/
F: Ad Altare unius Virginis | At the altar of one Virgin
G: op-abl-a32 | Veni, elécta mea · Antiphona VI
T: {℣.} Diffúsa est grátia in lábiis tuis. {℟.} Proptérea benedíxit te Deus in ætérnum.
 = {℣.} Grace is poured abroad in thy lips. {℟.} Therefore hath God blessed thee for ever.
R: Si fuerit Virgo et Martyr
 = If she was a Virgin and Martyr
L: Orémus
 = Let us pray
T: ^Indulgéntiam nobis, quǽsumus, Dómine, beáta N. Virgo et Martyr implóret: quæ tibi grata semper éxstitit, et mérito castitátis, et tuæ professióne virtútis. Per Christum.
 = May blessed N., Virgin and Martyr, implore pardon for us, we beseech thee, O Lord: for she was ever pleasing to thee, both by the merit of her chastity and by the confession of thy power. Through Christ.
R: Si fuerit Virgo tantum
 = If she was a Virgin only
L: Orémus
 = Let us pray
T: ^Exáudi nos, Deus salutáris noster: ut sicut de beátæ N. Vírginis tuæ commemoratióne gaudémus; ita piæ devotiónis erudiámur afféctu. Per Christum.
 = Hear us, O God our Saviour, that as we rejoice in the commemoration of blessed N. thy Virgin, so we may be taught the affection of loving devotion. Through Christ.
R: Si fuerit Vidua
 = If she was a Widow
L: Orémus
 = Let us pray
T: ^Tuórum corda fidélium, Deus miserátor, illústra: et beátæ N. précibus gloriósis fac nos próspera mundi despícere, et cælésti semper consolatióne gaudére. Per Christum.
 = Enlighten, O merciful God, the hearts of thy faithful; and by the glorious prayers of blessed N. make us despise the prosperity of the world and ever rejoice in heavenly consolation. Through Christ.
F/
